  "narrative": "During a formation flying practice over Crowland, Lincolnshire, two Lancasters from 97 Squadron — ME265 and ND981 — suffered a catastrophic mid-air collision. Flight Lieutenant Van Raalte, an Australian, was piloting one of the aircraft when the two bombers struck each other. The collision left no opportunity for survival from either crew. In total, thirteen men were killed across both Lancasters. The squadron was based at RAF Coningsby at the time of the accident.",
